[center][size=6][b][color=#FCEE0A]CyberCAT-SimpleGUI[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4]Save editor for Cyberpunk 2077 — patch 2.5 and Phantom Liberty[/size][/center]

[line]

A maintained continuation of [url=https://github.com/Deweh/CyberCAT-SimpleGUI]Deweh's CyberCAT-SimpleGUI[/url], the classic save editor that stopped working with recent patches. It reads and writes [b]patch 2.5 saves[/b], including the new optimized stats format, and adds a lot on top: a perks editor for the 2.0 skill trees, a ripperdoc-style cyberware screen, a save browser, undo/redo and safer saving.

[b]Everything was tested in-game on a 2.5 save, including saving again from the game afterwards.[/b]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#00F0FF]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Saves[/b]
[list]
[*]Save browser with screenshots — double click a save to open it
[*]Safe saving: the file is verified before it replaces [i]sav.dat[/i], and the last 5 versions are kept as timestamped backups
[*]Warning on unsaved changes, a [b]*[/b] next to the save name, [b]Ctrl+S[/b] to save
[*][b]Undo/redo[/b] with [b]Ctrl+Z[/b] / [b]Ctrl+Y[/b] (up to 10 steps)
[*]Saves from game versions newer than the editor supports open read-only, so they can't be damaged
[/list]

[b]Character[/b]
[list]
[*]Level, Street Cred, attributes, skills, attribute / perk / Relic points, life path
[*][b]Perks[/b]: every 2.0 skill tree and the Relic perks — unlock, max out or remove, with or without spending points
[/list]

[b]Cyberware[/b]
[list]
[*]Ripperdoc-style screen: body map, slot cards with icons and tiers, capacity and armor gauges
[*]Equip any cyberware in any slot of its body area, even items you don't own (they're created for you)
[*][b]Raise the cyberware capacity[/b] beyond the game's limit
[/list]

[b]Inventory[/b]
[list]
[*]In-game item names (English or Brazilian Portuguese), rarity colors for fixed-quality items
[*]Search with filters: [i]name: type: id: slot: quantity: desc:[/i]
[*]Add any item, copy/paste and clone items (with their mods and stats)
[*]Move items between V's inventory and the stash, one by one or everything listed
[*][b]Make Tier 5++[/b] and [b]Set Quantity[/b], also in bulk
[*]Crafting components editor, money
[*]Item details: quantity, flags, mod tree and stats
[/list]

[b]World[/b]
[list]
[*]Unlock or lock any player vehicle (search, unlock all / lock all)
[*]Unlock every fast travel point, including Dogtown
[*]Quest facts editor
[*]Appearance presets (load / save) and an advanced appearance editor
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#00F0FF]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit
[*][b]Standalone[/b] download (recommended): nothing else to install
[*]Regular download: needs the [url=https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download/dotnet/10.0].NET 10 Desktop Runtime (x64)[/url]
[/list]

This is a standalone program, not a game mod: it doesn't go into the game folder and isn't installed with a mod manager.

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#00F0FF]How to use[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close the game, or at least go back to the main menu
[*]Extract the zip anywhere and run [b]CP2077SaveEditor.exe[/b]
[*]Double click a save in the save browser
[*]Make your changes, then click [b]Save[/b] (or Ctrl+S) to overwrite that save, or [b]Save As...[/b] to write it into another save folder
[*]Load the save in the game
[/list]

[b]Tip:[/b] make a manual save in the game and edit that one. The editor keeps backups, but having a spare save never hurts.

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#00F0FF]Good to know[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Undo takes a few seconds[/b]: it reloads the whole save to go back a step
[*]Rarity colors only show for items whose rarity is fixed (mods, programs, cyberware...). Weapons and clothing roll their tier in the game, so they stay uncolored
[*]Gigs and NCPD activities can't be completed by the editor: their progress lives in the quest journal
[*]Saves with data from some game mods may not load; the error message says so when that's the case
[*]If something goes wrong, the details are in the [i]logs[/i] folder next to the exe — please attach that file to bug reports
[/list]

[b]Settings[/b] (optional [i]config.json[/i] next to the exe):
[list]
[*][i]"Theme": 1[/i] — classic light look; [i]"Theme": 0[/i] follows the Windows setting
[*][i]"UndoSteps": 0[/i] — turns undo off (each step keeps ~4 MB in memory)
[*][i]"CheckForUpdates": 0[/i] — no update check on startup
[/list]

